frontend: react
backend: python
db: sqlite
caching: redis(file based)


Phase 1: 

onboarding page:
    - ask user name and email for notification purposes
    - ask user to focus on physique or overall health and wellness/skin-care/hair-care (multi selections), food planning is mandotory, (make field optionol as per user selection)
    - provide photos of items you have in your home (optional, if not provided assume person is using zym, has most of the euqipments)
    - your full picture a shirtless is recommended for better fitting suggestions.
    - target body focus: give multiple options for body focus areas (e.g., arms, legs, torso) to tailor suggestions (multi selections + custom input for specific areas).
    - food preferences(optional): allow users to select dietary preferences (e.g., vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free) and any allergies.
    - ask user to provide their current weight, height, and age for personalized recommendations.
    - ask user to provide their current fitness level (beginner, intermediate, advanced) to tailor the workout plan accordingly.
    - ask user to provide their current skin type and hair type for personalized skin-care and hair-care routines, (make it optional)

    submit button: "Prepare Planning"

    once submitted:
        - we will use openai as llm, option to extend to other llms in future.
        two agents will be created:
            - agent 1: responsible for generating a personalized workout plan based on the user's inputs.
            - agent 2: responsible for generating a personalized meal plan based on the user's dietary preferences and allergies.
            - agent 3: skin-care routine and hair-care routine based on user's preferences and skin/hair type. [we will skip first 2 weeks for this unless user wants to start early]
            - agent 4: review them and critique and provide feedback on the generated plans to ensure they are balanced and effective, if any major suggestions required, they will be sent back to the respective agents for revision, max loop count will 3 for each task.
        
        - we will plan for first 4 weeks only first [idea is to understand user habits and preferences and how focused he is ?]
        - once food plan and workout plan are finalized, they will be sent to the user on dashboard and also store in db.
    - food plan:
        plan calory consumption and burn targets based on user's body focus areas and dietary preferences.

Planning:
    calendar view:
        - treat each meal/exercise plan as a task with a specific time and date.
        - user will mark them as completed or skipped.
        - based on that we will track user's adherence to the plan and provide feedback on their progress.
        - user should be able to see their progress over time with visual graphs and statistics.
        - a simple page for each day with horizontal scrollable list as date on top and selected date's plan below with option to mark as completed or skipped with all graphs  extra for that day.
        - home page will mention the current day plan and progress summary with a link to the calendar view for detailed tracking.
    

Refine current plan:
    on clickbutton --> ask for one input box and which will get stored as user preferences for future plan generation, and will be used to refine the current plan for next x days (max 4 week plan), and will be sent to the user on dashboard and also store in db.
Extend Plan:
    on clickbutton --> ask for one input box and which will get stored as user preferences for future plan generation, and will be used to extend the current plan for next x days (max 4 week plan), and will be sent to the user on dashboard and also store in db.


Admin page:
    - all the static pages will list over there.
    - with a tab static pages.

Phase 2 (MCP support):
    - it will provide a mcp server to allow users to connect from agents like claude-cli, chatgpt etc..
    - following things will be exposed, regenerate plan for next x days (max  4 week plan), get current day plan, get progress summary, mark task as completed or skipped, get detailed tracking for a specific date

    - for each day i can upload some of the photos to monitor how i am progressing, and the system will provide feedback on my progress based on the photos and my adherence to the plan.
